ngle-line with ellipsis on overflow).","name":"cardholder_name","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Optional accessible label override for the masked number (defaults to "Card ending in {last4}").","name":"masked_number_aria_label","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Whether to apply the overflow behavior: cardholder name single-line with end ellipsis and title containing full name; masked number and expiry remain single-line and do not wrap.","name":"enable_overflow_rules","required":false,"type":"boolean"}],"componentCode":"card_details","componentName":"Card Details","returns":[]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Stable identifier for the payment method represented by this delete control (used to request deletion and correlate results).","name":"payment_method_id","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Last 4 digits of the card number, used for accessible naming (e.g., "Delete card ending in 1234") and confirmation copy context.","name":"last4","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Card brand for confirmation copy context (e.g., "Visa"). If unknown, pass "Card" to match the fallback decision.","name":"card_brand","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Whether deletion is allowed. When false, render as a native disabled button and do not open the confirmation modal.","name":"can_delete","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Tooltip/title text shown when deletion is disabled (e.g., "You don’t have permission to delete this card").","name":"disabled_reason","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Whether a deletion request is currently in progress for this card; disables the button and swaps content to a spinner while preserving width.","name":"is_deleting","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user activates the delete button (before confirmation). Parent should open the confirmation modal/dialog.","name":"on_request_delete","required":true,"type":"(payload: RequestDeletePaymentCardPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user confirms deletion in the confirmation modal/dialog. Parent should execute the deletion request.","name":"on_confirm_delete","required":true,"type":"(payload: ConfirmDeletePaymentCardPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user cancels the confirmation modal/dialog. Parent should close the modal and return focus to the delete button.","name":"on_cancel_delete","required":true,"type":"(payload: CancelDeletePaymentCardPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user activates the inline "Retry" affordance after a deletion failure. Parent should retry the deletion request.","name":"on_retry_delete","required":false,"type":"(payload: RetryDeletePaymentCardPayload) => void"}],"componentCode":"delete_card_action","componentName":"Delete Card Action","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when the user activates the delete button (pre-confirmation) to request opening the confirmation modal/dialog.","name":"request_delete","required":true,"type":"RequestDeletePaymentCardPayload"},{"description":"Emitted when the user confirms deletion in the confirmation modal/dialog.","name":"confirm_delete","required":true,"type":"ConfirmDeletePaymentCardPayload"},{"description":"Emitted when the user cancels the confirmation modal/dialog.","name":"cancel_delete","required":true,"type":"CancelDeletePaymentCardPayload"},{"description":"Emitted when the user triggers a retry after a deletion error (if retry UI is shown).","name":"retry_delete","required":false,"type":"RetryDeletePaymentCardPayload"}]}],"relatedComponentSourceFiles":[{"componentCode":"card_brand_icon","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/CardBrandIcon/CardBrandIcon.tsx"},{"componentCode":"card_details","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/CardDetails/CardDetails.tsx"},{"componentCode":"delete_card_action","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/DeleteCardAction/DeleteCardAction.tsx"}],"resolvingGaps":{"decisions":[{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"selection_semantics_radio_card","decision":"Implement selection as a single-select radio pattern: the payment_card root renders with role="radio", aria-checked reflecting selected state, and is focusable with tabIndex=0 when enabled. Enter and Space on the focused payment_card trigger select_payment_card. If used outside a group, it still uses the same semantics but does not assume arrow-key navigation.","rationale":"This resolves the missing keyboard interaction model and clarifies that the card is selectable as a mutually exclusive option, which is common for saved payment method selection. Using role="radio" with aria-checked provides clear assistive-tech semantics while keeping implementation conservative and testable without introducing additional components not in scope.","sourceGap":"No defined keyboard interaction model for selecting the card (role, tab stop, Enter/Space behavior) versus activating the delete action"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"tab_order_card_then_delete","decision":"Define tab order as two stops: (1) payment_card container (select), then (2) delete_card_action button. The delete action must be a native <button type="button"> (or equivalent) and must not be reachable by tab before the card container.","rationale":"This explicitly separates selection from deletion in keyboard navigation, preventing accidental destructive activation and making interactions predictable. It also aligns with standard accessibility expectations and is straightforward to validate in tests.","sourceGap":"No defined keyboard interaction model for selecting the card (role, tab stop, Enter/Space behavior) versus activating the delete action"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["delete_card_action"],"code":"delete_button_accessible_name","decision":"If delete is icon-only, set aria-label to "Delete card ending in {last4}". If a visible label is present, keep it as visible text and do not add redundant aria-label; instead, ensure the visible text is "Delete" and append visually-hidden context "card ending in {last4}" for screen readers.","rationale":"This ensures the delete control has a unique, descriptive accessible name, particularly when multiple cards are listed. Using last4 is minimally identifying and avoids ambiguity while staying consistent with the masked display requirement.","sourceGap":"No accessible name/aria-label guidance for the delete action, especially if it is icon-only"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["card_details"],"code":"masked_number_sr_text","decision":"Render the visible masked number as "•••• •••• •••• 1234" (or "**** **** **** 1234"), but provide an aria-label (or dedicated screen-reader-only text) for the number field as "Card ending in 1234" so assistive tech does not read each mask character.","rationale":"This prevents verbose or confusing announcements of mask characters while still communicating the identifying last 4 digits. It is conservative because it does not expose the full PAN and uses a simple, consistent phrase for localization.","sourceGap":"No screen-reader text strategy for masked card number (how to announce last 4 digits and avoid reading asterisks literally)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"focus_visible_requirements","decision":"Apply visible focus styling to both the payment_card container and the delete_card_action button using :focus-visible. The focus indicator must be at least a 2px outline (or ring) with a 2px offset from the component boundary and must not rely on color alone (e.g., include outline/ring, not only background change).","rationale":"This directly resolves the lack of focus-visible requirements and provides an implementable, testable rule that works across themes. Using :focus-visible is conservative and avoids showing focus on mouse clicks while preserving keyboard accessibility.","sourceGap":"No focus-visible styling requirements for card container and delete control"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"prevent_select_on_delete","decision":"Clicking or pressing Enter/Space on delete_card_action must not trigger select_payment_card. Implement by stopping event propagation from delete_card_action to payment_card and ensuring the delete button is not nested inside an element with implicit click-to-select behavior that captures activation (or handle onClick on the container with target checks).","rationale":"This resolves activation conflicts between select and delete for both pointer and keyboard interactions. It is conservative because it does not require new UI patterns—only an explicit event contract and DOM structure discipline.","sourceGap":"No guidance to prevent click/activation conflicts between selecting the card and clicking delete (e.g., stopPropagation) with accessible semantics"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["card_brand_icon"],"code":"brand_icon_a11y","decision":"Treat card_brand_icon as decorative when the brand is also provided as text to assistive tech elsewhere; otherwise, set accessible name on the icon as the brand value (e.g., "Visa"). Concretely: default to aria-hidden="true" for the icon and include brand in the payment_card accessible name/description string as "Visa card ending in 1234".","rationale":"This avoids duplicate announcements while ensuring the brand is still conveyed when needed. Defaulting to decorative is conservative and reduces noise, while moving brand to a single accessible string improves consistency across icon asset variants.","sourceGap":"No indication of how the card brand icon is announced (decorative vs labeled with brand name)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card"],"code":"selected_state_styling","decision":"When selected, payment_card must show a clear selected indicator: a 2px border in the primary accent color plus a subtle selected background tint. Additionally, expose selection via aria-checked="true" per the radio semantics.","rationale":"This resolves the missing selected state and ensures both visual and non-visual users can determine the current selection. Border+tint is a minimal, common pattern that remains legible in dense lists.","sourceGap":"Selected state styling/indicator for the currently selected card"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"hover_pressed_states","decision":"Define interactive states: payment_card hover increases elevation by one step (or applies a subtle hover background) and pressed applies a slight scale-down (e.g., 0.99) or darker background; delete_card_action hover applies a background wash and pressed applies a darker wash. These states must not be the only indicator of focus (focus-visible remains separate).","rationale":"This fills in missing hover/pressed behavior with conservative, widely used affordances without needing exact token names. Separating focus from hover ensures accessibility and consistent behavior across input modes.","sourceGap":"Hover/pressed states for the card container and delete action"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["delete_card_action"],"code":"delete_disabled_state","decision":"Support a disabled delete state: when deletion is not allowed, render delete_card_action as disabled (disabled attribute for <button>) with tooltip/title text "You don’t have permission to delete this card" and keep it focusable only if the product already uses focusable-disabled patterns; otherwise remove from tab order via native disabled behavior.","rationale":"This addresses the missing disabled state with a default that is compatible with native controls and predictable for accessibility. Providing a short explanation via title/tooltip is a minimal addition that reduces confusion.","sourceGap":"Disabled state for delete (e.g., insufficient permissions, locked payment method)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["delete_card_action","payment_card"],"code":"delete_confirmation_modal","decision":"Require confirmation before deletion using a modal dialog. Dialog copy: title "Delete payment method?" body "This will remove {brand} card ending in {last4} from your saved payment methods." Primary button "Delete" (destructive styling) and secondary "Cancel". On confirm, trigger delete_payment_card; on cancel, close dialog and return focus to delete_card_action.","rationale":"This resolves the missing confirmation state with a standard, accessible pattern that reduces accidental destructive actions. It is conservative because it avoids inline popovers that can be harder to implement accessibly and ensures clear focus management.","sourceGap":"Delete confirmation state (dialog/popover) to prevent accidental destructive action"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["delete_card_action"],"code":"deletion_in_progress_state","decision":"During deletion in progress, disable delete_card_action and replace its icon/label with a small inline spinner while preserving the button width. Also set aria-busy="true" on payment_card to signal the busy state to assistive tech.","rationale":"This defines a concrete loading behavior that prevents duplicate submissions and provides clear feedback. Using aria-busy on the card is a minimal accessibility improvement without introducing new announcement systems.","sourceGap":"Deletion in-progress state (loading/spinner, delete button disabled)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action"],"code":"deletion_error_feedback","decision":"On deletion failure, keep the card visible, re-enable delete_card_action, and show an inline error message within payment_card: "Couldn’t delete this payment method. Try again." Provide a "Retry" affordance that triggers delete_payment_card again and ensure the error region has role="alert".","rationale":"This resolves the missing error state with a local, testable feedback mechanism that does not depend on global toast infrastructure. role="alert" ensures the failure is announced without extra complexity.","sourceGap":"Deletion error state (failure feedback and retry behavior)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["card_details"],"code":"long_text_overflow_rules","decision":"Cardholder name must be single-line with end ellipsis and a title attribute containing the full name. Masked number and expiry remain single-line and must not wrap. If localization causes label expansion, the details section truncates with ellipsis rather than wrapping.","rationale":"This resolves long-text overflow behavior with a conservative rule that preserves row height consistency in lists. The title attribute provides a minimal way to access full content without introducing additional UI.","sourceGap":"Long-text overflow state for cardholder name and localized labels"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["card_brand_icon"],"code":"unknown_brand_fallback","decision":"If card_brand is unknown/unsupported, render a generic card icon asset and set the brand text used in accessible strings to "Card" (e.g., "Card ending in 1234"). Do not omit the icon slot to avoid layout shifts.","rationale":"This addresses the fallback state while keeping layout stable and avoiding missing content. Using a generic label is conservative and avoids incorrect brand announcements.","sourceGap":"Unknown/unsupported card brand fallback state (generic icon or text)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["payment_card","delete_card_action","card_details","card_brand_icon"],"code":"small_width_layout","decision":"For narrow containers (<360px), keep a single-row layout: brand icon left, details in the middle, delete action right. Details area truncates (no wrapping) and the delete action remains pinned to the right. If space becomes insufficient, cardholder name is the first field to truncate, then masked number; expiry remains visible.","rationale":"This resolves responsive layout ambiguity without introducing a second layout mode that could increase complexity. Prioritizin