at is considered completed (inclusive). Steps with index <= this value are navigable; future steps should be aria-disabled="true".","name":"max_completed_step_index","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Accessible label applied to the underlying <ol> (e.g., "KYC steps").","name":"aria_label","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Responsive rendering mode. "condensed" renders e.g. "1/3" plus current step name; "full" renders horizontal step labels/buttons.","name":"variant","required":false,"type":""condensed" | "full""},{"description":"Called when the user clicks a step button (including current or completed steps). Parent should enforce 'no jumping forward' and ignore disallowed indices.","name":"on_step_click","required":false,"type":"(payload: KycStepIndicatorStepClickPayload) => void"}],"componentCode":"kyc_step_indicator","componentName":"Step indicator","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when a step button is activated. Used by the parent wizard to navigate to an allowed (completed/current) step.","name":"step_click","required":true,"type":"KycStepIndicatorStepClickPayload"}]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Whether the personal info step is currently the active step being displayed. Used to control focus behavior and aria visibility in the parent wizard layout.","name":"is_active","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Text for the step heading (rendered as an <h2> and used as the focus target on step entry).","name":"step_title","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Stable id attribute for the step heading element (<h2>). The parent wizard uses this to move focus to the heading on successful step transitions.","name":"step_heading_id","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Current value of the required confirmation checkbox: "I confirm the above information is correct".","name":"is_confirmed","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether the step is currently blocked by a validation error (used to set aria-invalid on the checkbox and to render inline error UI). Typically true when Next was attempted while is_confirmed is false.","name":"has_error","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Inline error message to show for the confirmation checkbox when has_error is true (also referenced via aria-describedby).","name":"error_message","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Id of the element containing the inline error message for the checkbox. When has_error is true, this id should be included in the checkbox aria-describedby (in addition to any other described-by ids).","name":"error_message_id","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Callback fired when the user toggles the confirmation checkbox.","name":"on_confirm_change","required":true,"type":"(checked: boolean) => void"},{"description":"Callback fired when the step needs focus moved to the first invalid control (the confirmation checkbox), typically after a failed Next attempt. Parent can use this for deterministic focus management across steps.","name":"on_request_focus_invalid","required":false,"type":"() => void"}],"componentCode":"personal_info_step","componentName":"Personal info step","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when the confirmation checkbox value changes.","name":"confirm_change","required":true,"type":"boolean"}]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Heading text for step 2, used as the focus target on step entry (rendered as an <h2> with tabIndex="-1").","name":"step_title","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Whether this step is the currently active step in the wizard (controls visibility/aria-busy scope when active).","name":"is_active","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether navigation is temporarily locked due to an async Next/submit action (Back/Next disabled upstream); used to disable interactions in this step and set aria-busy="true" on the step container when active.","name":"is_busy","required":false,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Currently selected document items and their UI/upload states (empty/selected/uploading/success/failure) to render the list and error states.","name":"documents","required":true,"type":"KycDocumentUploadItem[]"},{"description":"Accepted MIME types for document files (used for validation and for the underlying file input accept attribute).","name":"accepted_mime_types","required":true,"type":"string[]"},{"description":"Maximum allowed size per document file in bytes (10MB). Used for client-side validation and user messaging.","name":"max_file_size_bytes","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Maximum number of document files allowed (3). Used for client-side validation and user messaging.","name":"max_file_count","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Whether the step currently satisfies the blocking requirement for proceeding (at least one successfully uploaded document).","name":"is_step_valid","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Blocking error message shown/announced when the user tries to proceed but the step is invalid (used by step-level aria-live assertive region and linked via aria-describedby to the relevant control).","name":"blocking_error","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Non-blocking error messages (e.g., rejected files: unsupported type, too large, duplicate, max count exceeded) to display as an inline error summary and reference from controls for accessibility.","name":"upload_errors","required":false,"type":"KycUploadError[]"},{"description":"Instruction text for the upload area, referenced by aria-describedby on the dropzone and file input (must include accepted formats, max size, and max count).","name":"instructions_text","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user adds files via file picker or drag-and-drop. Parent performs validation (type/size/duplicates/max count), updates documents state, and may start auto-upload.","name":"on_add_files","required":true,"type":"(files: File[], source: "picker" | "drop") => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user removes a previously selected/uploaded file from the list.","name":"on_remove_file","required":true,"type":"(document_id: string) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user retries upload for a failed file.","name":"on_retry_upload","required":false,"type":"(document_id: string) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the step becomes ready to proceed (e.g., after documents update); useful for parent to clear wizard-level blocking errors.","name":"on_step_validity_change","required":false,"type":"(is_valid: boolean) => void"}],"componentCode":"document_upload_step","componentName":"Document upload step","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when user selects or drops files in this step, providing the raw File objects and the interaction source for analytics/telemetry or validation handling.","name":"files_added","required":true,"type":"{ files: File[]; source: "picker" | "drop" }"},{"description":"Emitted when user removes a document from the step.","name":"file_removed","required":true,"type":"{ document_id: string }"},{"description":"Emitted when user retries a failed upload from the step.","name":"upload_retried","required":false,"type":"{ document_id: string }"},{"description":"Emitted when the step validity changes (e.g., first successful upload makes it valid; removal makes it invalid).","name":"step_validity_changed","required":false,"type":"{ is_valid: boolean }"}]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Whether the selfie step is currently the active visible step in the wizard (used for rendering and focus management expectations).","name":"is_active","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether the overall wizard/step container is in an async busy state (e.g., Next triggered submission); used to disable controls and set aria-busy on the step container.","name":"is_busy","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Heading text for the step (rendered as an <h2> with tabIndex="-1" to receive focus on step entry).","name":"step_heading","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Stable DOM id for the step heading element (used by parent for focus management and by aria-labelledby on the step container).","name":"step_heading_id","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Instruction text shown near the upload control and referenced via aria-describedby on the file input and any upload trigger controls.","name":"upload_instructions","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"DOM id of the instructions element (referenced via aria-describedby).","name":"upload_instructions_id","required":true,"type":"string"},{"description":"Accepted MIME types for the selfie file picker (per decisions: image/jpeg and image/png).","name":"accepted_mime_types","required":true,"type":"string[]"},{"description":"Maximum allowed selfie file size in bytes (per decisions: 10MB).","name":"max_file_size_bytes","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Currently selected selfie file (null when none). Used to render the preview and determine validity.","name":"selfie_file","required":true,"type":"File | null"},{"description":"Preview URL for the selected selfie image (e.g., object URL). Null when no preview is available.","name":"selfie_preview_url","required":true,"type":"string | null"},{"description":"Validation/error message to show for the selfie control. When present, the input/control should be marked aria-invalid and this message id included in aria-describedby.","name":"error_message","required":false,"type":"string | null"},{"description":"DOM id for the error message element (referenced via aria-describedby when error_message is present).","name":"error_message_id","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Whether the selfie control is currently invalid (drives aria-invalid="true").","name":"is_invalid","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Callback fired when the user selects a new selfie file via the file picker (Replace uses the same path).","name":"on_select_selfie_file","required":true,"type":"(file: File) => void"},{"description":"Callback fired when the user removes/clears the current selfie selection.","name":"on_remove_selfie_file","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Callback fired when the user requests to replace the selfie (typically opens the file picker). Parent can implement by programmatically clicking the hidden input.","name":"on_request_replace","required":true,"type":"() => void"}],"componentCode":"selfie_step","componentName":"Selfie step","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when a new selfie file is chosen; payload includes the selected File object.","name":"selfie_file_selected","required":true,"type":"SelfieFileSelectedPayload"},{"description":"Emitted when the current selfie is cleared/removed.","name":"selfie_file_removed","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Emitted when the user activates the Replace action to choose a different file (request to open picker).","name":"replace_requested","required":true,"type":"() => void"}]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Zero-based current wizard step index used to render Back/Next disabled/loading states (0=personal info, 1=document upload, 2=selfie).","name":"current_step_index","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Total number of steps in the wizard (expected to be 3). Used to determine whether Next is available on the last step.","name":"total_steps","required":true,"type":"number"},{"description":"Whether navigating backward is currently allowed. When false, Back renders disabled (e.g., step 1 or during async submit).","name":"can_go_back","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether navigating forward is currently allowed. When false, Next renders disabled (e.g., step invalid, uploads incomplete, or during async submit).","name":"can_go_next","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether the wizard is currently performing an async action triggered by Next (e.g., upload/submit). When true, Next shows loading and both controls should be disabled.","name":"is_submitting","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Optional label override for the Back button text (default: "Back").","name":"back_label","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Optional label override for the Next button text (default: "Next").","name":"next_label","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Called when the user activates Back. Parent is responsible for performing navigation and focus management.","name":"on_back","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Called when the user activates Next. Parent is responsible for validation/submit, navigation, and focus management.","name":"on_next","required":true,"type":"() => void"}],"componentCode":"wizard_navigation","componentName":"Wizard navigation","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when the Back control is activated.","name":"back","required":true,"type":"void"},{"description":"Emitted when the Next control is activated.","name":"next","required":true,"type":"void"}]},{"accepts":[{"description":"Verification status value to render. Use "pending_review", "approved", or "rejected"; any other non-null value should render the "Status unavailable" fallback.","name":"status","required":false,"type":"KycVerificationStatus | null"},{"description":"Whether the status is currently being fetched; when true, render the loading UI (e.g., "Loading status...").","name":"is_loading","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether the latest status fetch failed; when true, render the error UI (e.g., "Unable to load status") with a Retry action.","name":"has_error","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user clicks the Retry button in the error state to re-fetch status.","name":"on_retry","required":false,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Accessible label for the overall status region (used for screen readers).","name":"aria_label","required":false,"type":"string"}],"componentCode":"verification_status","componentName":"Verification status","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when the user requests a retry after a status-load failure (fires when Retry is activated).","name":"retry_requested","required":true,"type":"void"}]}],"relatedComponentSourceFiles":[{"componentCode":"kyc_step_indicator","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/KycStepIndicator/KycStepIndicator.tsx"},{"componentCode":"personal_info_step","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/PersonalInfoStep/PersonalInfoStep.tsx"},{"componentCode":"document_upload_step","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/DocumentUploadStep/DocumentUploadStep.tsx"},{"componentCode":"selfie_step","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/SelfieStep/SelfieStep.tsx"},{"componentCode":"wizard_navigation","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/WizardNavigation/WizardNavigation.tsx"},{"componentCode":"verification_status","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/VerificationStatus/VerificationStatus.tsx"}],"resolvingGaps":{"decisions":[{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","kyc_step_indicator"],"code":"step_indicator_semantics","decision":"Implement the step indicator as an ordered list (<ol>) with each step as a list item containing a <button type="button">. Apply aria-current="step" to the active step button, and set aria-disabled="true" on future step buttons (while still rendering them). The list has aria-label="KYC steps".","rationale":"Defines concrete screen-reader semantics for steps and the active step, and conservatively avoids overpromising navigation by disabling future steps by default while still conveying progress.","sourceGap":"Step indicator semantics not defined (aria-current for active step, progress/step list labeling for screen readers)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","kyc_step_indicator"],"code":"step_click_navigation_rules","decision":"Allow clicking step indicator buttons to navigate only to already-completed steps and the current step; disallow jumping forward. Completion is defined as having successfully advanced past a step at least once in the current session.","rationale":"Resolves ambiguity about whether step indicator is interactive while keeping a conservative KYC flow that prevents skipping required steps.","sourceGap":"Define wizard navigation rules (can users click step indicator to jump steps, can they skip steps, behavior when moving back after uploading files)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","personal_info_step","document_upload_step","selfie_step","wizard_navigation","back_button","next_button"],"code":"wizard_initial_state_and_back_button","decision":"Default initial state is step 1 (personal info) with no restoration of prior progress. Back button is rendered but disabled on step 1 (disabled attribute and aria-disabled="true").","rationale":"Unblocks deterministic initialization and first-step navigation behavior without introducing persistence requirements that are not specified.","sourceGap":"Initial wizard state not defined (which step is default, whether prior saved progress is restored)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","wizard_navigation","next_button","personal_info_step"],"code":"personal_info_min_validation","decision":"Implement minimal Next-gating on the personal info step: Next is enabled only when all fields in that step are valid; since fields are unspecified, implement the step as a required confirmation checkbox labeled "I confirm the above information is correct" and require it checked to proceed.","rationale":"Creates an explicit, testable validation rule without inventing a full personal-info schema that is not present in the brief, while still enforcing a required action before progressing.","sourceGap":"Per-step form validation states not defined (required fields, format errors, blocking Next until valid)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","wizard_navigation","next_button","document_upload","document_upload_step","selfie_step"],"code":"async_next_loading_and_disable","decision":"When Next triggers an async action (document upload submission or selfie submission), set Next to loading and disabled (disabled attribute + aria-busy="true" on the step container); Back is also disabled during this period to prevent step changes mid-submit.","rationale":"Defines concrete disabled/loading behavior to prevent double submits and inconsistent wizard state during asynchronous operations.","sourceGap":"Next button disabled/loading state during uploads/submission not defined"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["document_upload"],"code":"document_upload_file_rules","decision":"Document upload accepts multiple files with a max count of 3. Validate each file client-side: type must be application/pdf, image/jpeg, or image/png; size must be <= 10MB. Duplicates are detected by (name, size, lastModified) and rejected with an error. Invalid files are not added to the selected list.","rationale":"Resolves multiple missing file-handling edge cases (count, duplicates, type/size validation) using conservative caps and deterministic duplicate detection suitable for tests.","sourceGap":"File validation error states not defined (unsupported type, >10MB, multiple files allowed or not, duplicate file handling)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["document_upload"],"code":"document_upload_states_and_progress","decision":"Document upload maintains explicit UI states: empty (no files), selected (files listed), uploading (per-file progress indicator shown as indeterminate unless actual progress is available), success (file marked uploaded), failure (file marked failed with retry action), and removed (file removed from list). Uploads start immediately upon selection/drop (auto-upload).","rationale":"Defines the missing upload lifecycle and whether uploads are immediate, enabling consistent UI generation and state-driven tests.","sourceGap":"Document upload states not defined (empty/no file selected, uploading progress, upload success, upload failure, file removed)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["document_upload"],"code":"drag_drop_active_reject_states","decision":"Dropzone supports drag states: idle, drag-over-accept, drag-over-reject. When dragging files over the dropzone, compute accept/reject based on the same type/size rules; apply a visible style change and announce "Files will be added" vs "Some files are not supported" via an aria-live="polite" region. On drop with rejected files, keep accepted files and show an inline error summary for rejected ones.","rationale":"Specifies hover/active/reject behavior and feedback for invalid drops while keeping acceptance rules consistent with picker validation.","sourceGap":"Drag-and-drop hover/active/reject states not defined (drag over highlight, dropping invalid file feedback)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["document_upload"],"code":"dropzone_keyboard_support","decision":"Make the dropzone focusable (tabIndex=0) and treat Enter/Space as opening the file picker. Also render a visible "Choose files" button inside the dropzone that triggers the same input. Do not require drag-and-drop for completion.","rationale":"Provides a keyboard-accessible path for file selection and defines exact key behavior, satisfying accessibility without changing core functionality.","sourceGap":"Keyboard interaction for drag-and-drop upload not specified (keyboard-accessible upload trigger, Enter/Space behavior on dropzone)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["document_upload","document_upload_step","selfie_step"],"code":"upload_accessible_instructions","decision":"Add a static instruction text element for each upload area and reference it with aria-describedby on the file input and dropzone. Document upload instruction text must include: "Accepted formats: PDF, JPG, PNG. Max size: 10MB. Up to 3 files."","rationale":"Defines accessible names/instructions and ensures constraints are communicated consistently to assistive technologies.","sourceGap":"File upload and selfie upload accessible names/instructions not specified (label text, accepted formats, max size communicated via aria-describedby)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","personal_info_step","document_upload_step","document_upload","selfie_step"],"code":"error_accessibility_contract","decision":"For field/file errors: set aria-invalid="true" on the invalid input/control and include the error message id in aria-describedby (appending to any existing described-by). Additionally, provide a step-level aria-live="assertive" error region that announces the first blocking error when Next is pressed and validation fails.","rationale":"Defines explicit linking between errors and controls and provides deterministic announcement behavior for validation and upload failures.","sourceGap":"Error messaging accessibility not specified (inline errors linked to fields/files with aria-invalid and aria-describedby, live region for upload errors)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","personal_info_step","document_upload_step","selfie_step","wizard_navigation"],"code":"focus_management_on_step_change","decision":"On successful Next/Back step transition, move focus to the step heading (an <h2> with tabIndex="-1"). On failed validation, move focus to the first invalid control in the current step; if none is focusable, focus the step-level error region.","rationale":"Removes ambiguity about focus behavior, supports keyboard users, and enables predictable automated accessibility testing.","sourceGap":"Focus management between steps not specified (where focus lands after Next/Back, preserving focus on validation errors)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["selfie_step"],"code":"selfie_collection_mode","decision":"Implement selfie step as a single image file upload (JPG/PNG only, max 10MB) with preview and actions: Replace (opens picker) and Remove (clears selection). Do not implement camera capture in this version.","rationale":"Resolves ambiguity about upload vs capture with the simplest implementation that aligns with the existing file-upload pattern and avoids additional device permission complexity.","sourceGap":"Selfie step upload/capture states not defined (whether it is file upload vs camera capture, preview, retake/remove)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","verification_status"],"code":"verification_status_loading_and_error","decision":"When entering the final status view, fetch status asynchronously and show a loading state (skeleton/text "Loading status..."). On fetch error, show "Unable to load status" with a Retry button that re-fetches. If status is not one of pending_review/approved/rejected, render "Status unavailable".","rationale":"Defines the missing retrieval states and ensures the UI handles unknown backend responses safely.","sourceGap":"Verification status retrieval states not defined (loading status, retry on fetch error, unknown/unavailable status)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["verification_status"],"code":"status_non_color_cues","decision":"Each status renders an icon plus text, not color alone: pending shows a clock icon and "Pending review"; approved shows a check icon and "Approved"; rejected shows an alert icon and "Rejected". Color is supplemental only.","rationale":"Ensures status meaning is conveyed without relying on color, addressing color-blind and contrast scenarios conservatively.","sourceGap":"Verification status relies on color mapping without non-color cues specified (icons/text patterns to meet color-contrast and color-blind needs)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["kyc_verification_wizard","kyc_step_indicator","wizard_navigation","document_upload"],"code":"responsive_layout_rules","decision":"Wizard container max-width is 720px with 16px padding on mobile and 24px on >=768px; center aligned. Step indicator: on <360px, render condensed variant "1/3", "2/3", "3/3" with the current step name below; on >=360px, render horizontal steps and allow label wrapping to 2 lines with ellipsis after 2 lines. Navigation: on mobile, render a sticky bottom bar with Back and Next full-width stacked (Next above Back); on >=768px, render inline with Back left and Next right. Dropzone minimum height is 120px and instruction text wraps; tap targets (buttons) minimum height 44px.","rationale":"Resolves multiple responsive ambiguities (container, step indicator, button placement, dropzone sizing, truncation) with clear breakpoints and deterministic behavior.","sourceGap":"Overall wizard container constraints not defined (max width, padding, and how it behaves in embedded vs full-page contexts)"}]},"targetComponent":{"code":"kyc_verification_wizard","name":"KYC verification wizard","parentCode":null,"purpose":"Guide the user through KYC steps and show final verification status.","statePolicy":"smart","type":"wizard"},"targetComponentInterface":{"accepts":[{"description":"Optional initial step when the wizard mounts. Defaults to "personal_info" per gap-resolution decision.","name":"initial_step","required":false,"type":"KycWizardStep"},{"description":"Current active step controlled by the parent (if provided, wizard behaves as controlled for step navigation).","name":"current_step","required":false,"type":"KycWizardStep"},{"description":"Whether step 1 (personal info confirmation) is currently valid; used to enable/disable Next on step 1.","name":"is_personal_info_valid","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Document upload aggregate state needed to determine whether step 2 is valid and whether Next should be blocked (e.g., requires at least one successfully uploaded document).","name":"document_upload_state","required":true,"type":"DocumentUploadState"},{"description":"Whether the selfie selection for step 3 is currently valid (JPG/PNG <=10MB, and present). Used to enable/disable Next on step 3.","name":"is_selfie_valid","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Global async lock for the wizard when Next triggers an async action (document/selfie submission). When true, Next shows loading/disabled and Back is disabled; step container should be aria-busy.","name":"is_submitting","required":true,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Whether steps have been completed in the current session; used to allow step-indicator navigation only to completed/current steps and to aria-disable future steps.","name":"completed_steps","required":true,"type":"KycWizardStep[]"},{"description":"Verification status view state used when the wizard is in the final status view (loading, error, or resolved status).","name":"verification_status_state","required":true,"type":"VerificationStatusState"},{"description":"Callback when the user requests navigation to a different step (Back/Next or clicking a completed step in the step indicator).","name":"on_step_change","required":true,"type":"(payload: KycStepChangePayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback when Next is pressed. Parent should run validation/submit logic and update is_submitting and step/verification status state accordingly.","name":"on_next","required":true,"type":"(payload: KycNextPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback when Back is pressed.","name":"on_back","required":true,"type":"(payload: KycBackPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when Next is pressed but the current step is blocking due to validation/upload requirements; used to surface step-level aria-live errors and drive focus-to-first-error behavior.","name":"on_blocking_error","required":false,"type":"(payload: KycBlockingErrorPayload) => void"},{"description":"Callback to retry fetching verification status from the status view when status load fails.","name":"on_retry_status_fetch","required":false,"type":"() => void"}],"componentCode":"kyc_verification_wizard","componentName":"KYC verification wiz