      "code": "sortable_headers_as_buttons_with_aria_sort",
      "decision": "Implement each sortable column header as a <button type=\"button\"> inside the <th>. The button accessible name is \"Sort by {ColumnName}\". Maintain sort state in the table as {sortKey, sortDirection}. Apply aria-sort to the <th> of the active sort column only: \"ascending\" or \"descending\"; all other headers have no aria-sort attribute. The header button shows a visual sort indicator (up/down chevron) and includes visually-hidden text that announces \"sorted ascending/descending\" for the active column.",
      "rationale": "This makes sorting explicitly keyboard-operable and screen-reader discoverable using standard table semantics with aria-sort, while keeping the rest of the headers neutral. Using a button in the header is the most conservative, widely supported pattern for interactive sorting.",
      "sourceGap": "Sorting controls are not specified as keyboard-operable header buttons with proper aria-sort and accessible names"
    },
    {
      "affectedComponentCodes": [
