      "code": "sort_state_defaults_and_toggle_behavior",
      "decision": "Default sort is Date descending on initial render. Sorting is single-column only (no multi-sort). Clicking/activating a header toggles direction between ascending and descending for that column; selecting a different column sets that column to ascending on first activation. There is no unsorted state once data is shown.",
      "rationale": "Defines deterministic sorting behavior needed for implementation and testing. Choosing a common default (most recent first) and a simple two-state toggle avoids ambiguous \"none\" state handling and multi-sort complexity.",
