g on sort/paginate)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"empty_state_rendering","decision":"If there are zero transactions after loading completes, render an empty state in the table body area that spans all columns with message: "No transactions to display." Keep the table header visible and keep pagination hidden/disabled when total count is 0.","rationale":"Provides a clear, minimal empty state without inventing filtering or onboarding content. Keeping headers visible maintains context and reduces layout shift.","sourceGap":"Table empty state when there are no transactions"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"error_state_with_retry","decision":"If data fetch fails, render an error state in the table body area spanning all columns with message: "Unable to load transactions." Provide a "Retry" button that re-attempts the last request (same sort/page/pageSize).","rationale":"Defines an actionable error path and a deterministic retry behavior needed for implementation and automated tests, without adding extra recovery flows.","sourceGap":"Table error state when data fetch fails (and retry behavior)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"row_interactive_hover_pressed_styles","decision":"For pointer users, rows show hover styling (subtle background change) indicating clickability. When the row’s "View details" control is active/pressed, show a pressed state on that control (not on the entire row). No persistent "selected" row state is used in the table.","rationale":"Resolves ambiguity around hover/active/selected states while avoiding introducing a selection model not mentioned in the brief.","sourceGap":"Row hover/active/selected state styling (especially for clickable rows)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_pagination"],"code":"pagination_model_and_total_count_requirement","decision":"Pagination is server-driven and requires totalCount from the data source. Compute totalPages = ceil(totalCount / pageSize). Display current page as "Page X of Y". If totalCount changes and the current page exceeds totalPages, clamp current page to totalPages and refetch.","rationale":"Defines a precise, testable pagination model and handles dynamic totals conservatively by clamping to the last valid page instead of erroring or showing empty pages unexpectedly.","sourceGap":"Define pagination model precisely: total count availability, total pages calculation, current page display format, and behavior when total changes"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_pagination"],"code":"pagination_controls_disabled_states","decision":"Provide First/Previous/Next/Last controls. Disable First and Previous when currentPage == 1. Disable Next and Last when currentPage == totalPages or totalPages == 0. Disabled controls are not focusable and use aria-disabled only if rendered as non-button elements; prefer native disabled buttons.","rationale":"Explicitly defines boundary behavior and a conservative accessibility-friendly implementation using native disabled semantics.","sourceGap":"Disabled/unavailable pagination states (first/prev disabled on first page; next/last disabled on last page)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_pagination"],"code":"page_size_change_resets_page","decision":"Page size selector offers 25, 50, 100. Changing page size resets currentPage to 1 and triggers a refetch with the current sort settings preserved. The selector reflects the active page size value.","rationale":"Resetting to page 1 is the most predictable behavior and avoids landing on an out-of-range page after a page size change.","sourceGap":"Page size change behavior state: whether changing page size resets to page 1 and how selection is reflected"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_pagination"],"code":"pagination_aria_labels_and_live_announcement","decision":"Add aria-labels: First="First page", Previous="Previous page", Next="Next page", Last="Last page". Page size select has label "Rows per page". Add an aria-live="polite" region that announces "Page {X} of {Y}" after pagination changes and "Sorted by {ColumnName} {Direction}" after sort changes.","rationale":"Resolves missing ARIA labeling and provides minimal announcements for state changes without overcomplicating the UI with verbose narration.","sourceGap":"Pagination controls lack defined ARIA labels (e.g., next/previous, page size selector, current page announcement)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table","transaction_pagination"],"code":"responsive_horizontal_scroll_and_column_overflow","decision":"On narrow viewports, keep the table layout (no card/stacked conversion) and enable horizontal scrolling by wrapping the table in an overflow-x:auto container. For Merchant Name and Payment Method cells, truncate with ellipsis (white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis) and show full content via native title attribute. Date, Amount, and Status do not wrap. No columns are hidden or reordered responsively.","rationale":"Chooses the least disruptive responsive strategy consistent with a table component and avoids speculative column priority/hiding rules. Ellipsis + title is a conservative overflow solution requiring no additional components.","sourceGap":"No rules for handling narrow viewports: whether columns wrap, truncate with ellipsis, or collapse into a stacked/card layout"}]},"unitTests":{"components":[{"componentCode":"transaction_status_badge","componentName":"Transaction Status Badge","coveredBehaviors":["Renders a non-color status text label for each supported status (pending/completed/failed/refunded).","Falls back to a neutral "Unknown" badge label when provided an unsupported status value.","Applies status-specific styling hooks (data-status and/or className) for supported statuses and unknown fallback."],"coveredStates":["Pending","Completed","Failed","Refunded","Unknown (unsupported status)"],"files":[{"filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/TransactionStatusBadge/TransactionStatusBadge.spec.tsx","content":"import React from 'react';
