pe":"open_details"}],"rootComponentCode":"transaction_table","specifiedStates":[],"tokenReferences":[{"componentCode":"transaction_status_badge","description":"Badge colors mapped per status (pending, completed, failed, refunded).","name":"status color","type":"color"}]},"projectRootPath":"/app/generated/frontend","relatedComponentInterfaces":[{"accepts":[{"description":"Transaction status value to render as a labeled, colored badge. Supported: "pending", "completed", "failed", "refunded". Unknown/unsupported values should render a neutral gray badge labeled "Unknown".","name":"status","required":true,"type":""pending" | "completed" | "failed" | "refunded" | string"},{"description":"Optional override for the displayed badge text. If omitted, the component derives the label from `status` (e.g., pending -> "Pending"), and uses "Unknown" for unsupported values.","name":"label","required":false,"type":"string"},{"description":"Optional accessible label override for assistive technologies. If omitted, aria-label matches the visible text label.","name":"aria_label","required":false,"type":"string"}],"componentCode":"transaction_status_badge","componentName":"Transaction Status Badge","returns":[]}],"relatedComponentSourceFiles":[{"componentCode":"transaction_status_badge","filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/TransactionStatusBadge/TransactionStatusBadge.tsx"}],"resolvingGaps":{"decisions":[{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"sortable_header_keyboard_and_aria_sort","decision":"Implement each sortable column header as a focusable button within the <th>. Support Enter/Space to toggle sorting on that column. Apply aria-sort on the corresponding <th> with values "none" (unsorted), "ascending", or "descending"; only the actively sorted column has ascending/descending and all others are "none".","rationale":"This defines a complete keyboard interaction and a standards-based announcement of sort state without changing the visual design requirements, enabling accessible sorting for all columns.","sourceGap":"Define keyboard interaction for sortable headers (tab focus, Enter/Space to sort) and announce sort state via aria-sort"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"row_details_accessible_action","decision":"Make the first cell in each row (Date) contain a full-row overlay anchor link styled to cover the row hit area. The link navigates to a details route pattern "/transactions/{transactionId}". The link accessible name is "View transaction {transactionId}". Preserve standard link behaviors (keyboard Enter, open in new tab via context menu/middle click).","rationale":"Using a real link provides a clear, keyboard-accessible affordance for opening details and supports common navigation expectations conservatively without inventing a modal/drawer pattern.","sourceGap":"Row click opens details but no accessible affordance is defined (e.g., row as link/button with role and accessible name) or alternative action for keyboard users"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"pagination_controls_labels_and_focus","decision":"Pagination includes: Previous button, Next button, and a page size <select> with options 25/50/100. Wrap controls in a <nav aria-label="Transaction table pagination">. Previous/Next have aria-label "Previous page" / "Next page" and use disabled=true at boundaries. Render current page text "Page X of Y" as an aria-live="polite" region that updates on page changes. Tab order is Previous -> Next -> Page size selector.","rationale":"This specifies explicit labels, boundary disabled behavior, and a deterministic focus order while keeping the UI minimal and consistent with the brief (no requirement for page numbers/first/last).","sourceGap":"Pagination controls need explicit labeling for screen readers (current page, next/previous, page size selector) and focus order behavior"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_status_badge"],"code":"status_badge_text_not_color_only","decision":"Always render the status text inside the badge (e.g., "Pending"). The badge element includes aria-label identical to the visible text. Do not rely on color to convey meaning; color is supplementary only.","rationale":"Keeping status text present ensures non-visual users receive the same information and resolves the risk of color-only encoding without requiring extra UI elements.","sourceGap":"Status conveyed by color only is possible; specify text/aria-label remains present and ensure badge meaning is announced non-visually"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table","transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"focus_visible_styles","decision":"Apply a consistent focus-visible ring to interactive elements: sortable header buttons, row overlay links, pagination buttons, and the page size select. Use a 2px outline with 2px offset and ensure it is visible on all status badge background colors.","rationale":"Explicit focus-visible styling ensures keyboard usability across all interactive controls without prescribing a full theme, and it is a conservative accessibility baseline.","sourceGap":"Specify focus-visible styling for interactive elements (headers, rows, pagination) to meet keyboard usability"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"loading_empty_error_states","decision":"Add three table-level states: (1) Loading: show 10-row skeleton placeholders while retaining the table header; disable sorting and pagination controls. (2) Empty: show a single full-width row message "No transactions"; keep headers visible and hide pagination. (3) Error: show a full-width message "Transactions couldn’t be loaded" with a "Retry" button that re-triggers fetch; keep headers visible and disable sorting/pagination until success.","rationale":"These states cover the primary data lifecycle gaps (loading/empty/error) in a way that preserves layout stability and defines control availability for downstream implementation and tests.","sourceGap":"