mezone, currency formatting for amount, right/left alignment, and negative/zero handling"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_status_badge"],"code":"status_to_style_mapping_and_unknown_fallback","decision":"Map statuses to badge styles: pending=amber, completed=green, failed=red, refunded=blue. Ensure text contrast meets WCAG AA for normal text. For unknown/unsupported status values, render a neutral gray badge with text "Unknown" and aria-label "Unknown".","rationale":"This provides an explicit mapping plus an accessible fallback, preventing rendering failures when new status values appear.","sourceGap":"Unknown/unsupported status value handling (fallback badge style/label)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"overflow_truncation_with_tooltips","decision":"Merchant Name and Payment Method cells are single-line with truncation (ellipsis). On hover and keyboard focus, show a tooltip containing the full text; the cell also includes a title attribute with the full value as a baseline fallback.","rationale":"This prevents layout breakage from long strings while still enabling access to the full content for mouse and keyboard users with a conservative fallback.","sourceGap":"Document data overflow behavior per column (truncate with ellipsis, wrap, tooltip on hover/focus) especially for merchant name and payment method"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table","transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"responsive_horizontal_scroll_and_min_widths","decision":"On small screens, keep the 5-column table and enable horizontal scrolling within a container (overflow-x:auto) rather than stacking/hiding columns. Set minimum widths: Date 120px, Amount 120px, Status 120px, Merchant Name 200px, Payment Method 160px. Pagination stays below the table; controls wrap to two lines if needed with page size selector on the second line.","rationale":"Horizontal scroll is the most conservative responsive strategy for dense tabular data, and minimum widths prevent