owed page size options for the page size selector. Expected to be [25, 50, 100].","name":"page_size_options","required":false,"type":"number[]"},{"description":"Whether pagination controls are disabled (e.g., while table is loading/sorting/paginating or in error state until success). When true, Previous/Next and page size selector are non-interactive.","name":"disabled","required":false,"type":"boolean"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user requests the previous page (via Previous button). Parent is responsible for updating current_page and fetching/rendering the new page.","name":"on_previous_page","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user requests the next page (via Next button). Parent is responsible for updating current_page and fetching/rendering the new page.","name":"on_next_page","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Callback invoked when the user changes the page size via the selector. Parent should reset to page 1 and keep current sort applied, then fetch/recompute data.","name":"on_page_size_change","required":true,"type":"(pageSize: number) => void"}],"componentCode":"transaction_table_pagination","componentName":"Transaction Table Pagination","returns":[{"description":"Emitted when the user activates the Previous button to request navigating to the previous page.","name":"previous_page_requested","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Emitted when the user activates the Next button to request navigating to the next page.","name":"next_page_requested","required":true,"type":"() => void"},{"description":"Emitted when the user selects a new page size (25/50/100). Payload is the selected page size.","name":"page_size_changed","required":true,"type":"(pageSize: number) => void"}]},"targetSourceFilePath":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/TransactionTablePagination/TransactionTablePagination.tsx","targetUnitTests":{"componentCode":"transaction_table_pagination","componentName":"Transaction Table Pagination","coveredBehaviors":["Renders pagination within a <nav> landmark labeled "Transaction table pagination"","Displays current page text "Page X of Y" and marks it aria-live="polite"","Previous/Next buttons have accessible names "Previous page" and "Next page"","Disables Previous button when current_page is 1","Disables Next button when current_page equals total_pages","Invokes on_previous_page when Previous is activated (when enabled)","Invokes on_next_page when Next is activated (when enabled)","Renders page size <select> with options 25/50/100 by default","Supports custom page_size_options prop for selector options","Invokes on_page_size_change with numeric payload when selection changes","When disabled=true, disables Previous/Next and page size selector and prevents callback invocations"],"coveredStates":["First page boundary (Previous disabled)","Last page boundary (Next disabled)","Middle page (Previous and Next enabled)","Disabled controls state","Default page size options","Custom page size options"],"files":[{"filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/TransactionTablePagination/TransactionTablePagination.spec.tsx","content":"import React from 'react';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import { TransactionTablePagination } from './TransactionTablePagination';

type Props = React.ComponentProps<typeof TransactionTablePagination>;

function renderComponent(override: Partial<Props> = {}) {
  const props: Props = {
    current_page: 1,
    total_pages: 3,
    page_size: 25,
    on_previous_page: jest.fn(),
    on_next_page: jest.fn(),
    on_page_size_change: jest.fn(),
    ...override
  };

  return {
    props,
    user: userEvent.setup(),
    ...render(<TransactionTablePagination {...props} />)
  };
}

describe('TransactionTablePagination', () => {
  it('renders within a nav landmark with an accessible label and exposes an aria-live page status', () => {
    renderComponent({ current_page: 2, total_pages: 5 });

    const nav = screen.getByRole('navigation', { name: /transaction table pagination/i });
    expect(nav).toBeInTheDocument();

    expect(screen.getByText('Page 2 of 5')).toBeInTheDocument();

    // Ensure the "Page X of Y" element is announced politely as it updates
    const pageStatus = screen.getByText('Page 2 of 5');
    expect(pageStatus).toHaveAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
  });

  it('sets correct accessible names for Previous/Next controls', () => {
    renderComponent({ current_page: 2, total_pages: 3 });

    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous page/i })).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next page/i })).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('disables Previous on first page and does not invoke callback when clicked', async () => {
    const { user, props } = renderComponent({ current_page: 1, total_pages: 3 });

    const prev = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous page/i });
    const next = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next page/i });

    expect(prev).toBeDisabled();
    expect(next).not.toBeDisabled();

    await user.click(prev);
    expect(props.on_previous_page).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });

  it('disables Next on last page and does not invoke callback when clicked', async () => {
    const { user, props } = renderComponent({ current_page: 4, total_pages: 4 });

    const prev = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous page/i });
    const next = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next page/i });

    expect(prev).not.toBeDisabled();
    expect(next).toBeDisabled();

    await user.click(next);
    expect(props.on_next_page).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });

  it('invokes on_previous_page and on_next_page when enabled', async () => {
    const { user, props } = renderComponent({ current_page: 2, total_pages: 4 });

    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous page/i }));
    expect(props.on_previous_page).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);

    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next page/i }));
    expect(props.on_next_page).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  it('renders default page size options (25/50/100) and selects the current page_size', () => {
    renderComponent({ page_size: 50 });

    const select = screen.getByRole('combobox');
    expect(select).toBeInTheDocument();

    const options = screen.getAllByRole('option').map((o) => (o as HTMLOptionElement).value);
    expect(options).toEqual(['25', '50', '100']);

    expect((select as HTMLSelectElement).value).toBe('50');
  });

  it('supports custom page_size_options', () => {
    renderComponent({ page_size: 50, page_size_options: [25, 50] });

    const options = screen.getAllByRole('option').map((o) => (o as HTMLOptionElement).value);
    expect(options).toEqual(['25', '50']);
  });

  it('invokes on_page_size_change with numeric payload when selection changes', async () => {
    const { user, props } = renderComponent({ page_size: 25 });

    const select = screen.getByRole('combobox');
    await user.selectOptions(select, '100');

    expect(props.on_page_size_change).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
    expect(props.on_page_size_change).toHaveBeenCalledWith(100);
  });

  it('when disabled=true, disables Previous/Next and the page size selector and prevents callback invocation', async () => {
    const { user, props } = renderComponent({ current_page: 2, total_pages: 4, disabled: true, page_size: 25 });

    const prev = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous page/i });
    const next = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next page/i });
    const select = screen.getByRole('combobox');

    expect(prev).toBeDisabled();
    expect(next).toBeDisabled();
    expect(select).toBeDisabled();

    await user.click(prev);
    await user.click(next);
    // Selecting options on a disabled select should not trigger change
    await user.selectOptions(select, '50');

    expect(props.on_previous_page).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
    expect(props.on_next_page).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
    expect(props.on_page_size_change).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});
