le ring to interactive elements: sortable header buttons, row overlay links, pagination buttons, and the page size select. Use a 2px outline with 2px offset and ensure it is visible on all status badge background colors.","rationale":"Explicit focus-visible styling ensures keyboard usability across all interactive controls without prescribing a full theme, and it is a conservative accessibility baseline.","sourceGap":"Specify focus-visible styling for interactive elements (headers, rows, pagination) to meet keyboard usability"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"loading_empty_error_states","decision":"Add three table-level states: (1) Loading: show 10-row skeleton placeholders while retaining the table header; disable sorting and pagination controls. (2) Empty: show a single full-width row message "No transactions"; keep headers visible and hide pagination. (3) Error: show a full-width message "Transactions couldn’t be loaded" with a "Retry" button that re-triggers fetch; keep headers visible and disable sorting/pagination until success.","rationale":"These states cover the primary data lifecycle gaps (loading/empty/error) in a way that preserves layout stability and defines control availability for downstream implementation and tests.","sourceGap":"Loading state for initial fetch and for sort/pagination transitions (skeleton/placeholder vs spinner)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"sort_behavior_defaults_and_nulls","decision":"Default sort is Date descending. Sorting is bi-state per column: selecting a column toggles ascending/descending; selecting a different column activates that column in ascending order. Sorting is stable. Null/blank values always sort last in both directions.","rationale":"This fully specifies predictable sort rules (default, toggling, stability, null handling) with conservative choices commonly used in transaction tables.","sourceGap":"Define sorting rules per column: default sort column/direction,