e supporting the required page sizes and clear user feedback.","sourceGap":"Specify pagination model: show total count, page count, and whether page size change resets to page 1; define available controls (first/prev/next/last, direct page input) and their labels"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"pagination_accessible_labels_and_live_updates","decision":"Add accessible labels: pagination nav has aria-label "Transaction pagination"; page size selector has label "Rows per page"; First/Prev/Next/Last buttons have aria-labels "First page", "Previous page", "Next page", "Last page". Add an aria-live="polite" status region within the table container that announces "Sorted by {column} {direction}" on sort and "Page {x} of {y}" on page changes.","rationale":"Explicit labeling and polite announcements address screen-reader discoverability and feedback for dynamic updates without overcomplicating the interaction model.","sourceGap":"Pagination controls lack labeling for screen readers (current page, total pages/results, page size selector label) and focus order expectations"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table","transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"focus_visible_requirements","decision":"Apply consistent :focus-visible styling to sortable header buttons, the "View details" control, and all pagination controls: 2px outline using the app focus color, 2px offset, and maintain at least 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors. Do not remove default outlines unless replaced by this rule.","rationale":"This creates a concrete, testable focus requirement for all interactive elements mentioned in the gaps and avoids relying on browser defaults that may be overridden by component styling.","sourceGap":"No focus-visible styling requirements specified for sortable headers, rows, and pagination controls"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_status_badge"],"code":"status_badge_contrast_and_noncolor_redundancy","decision":"Badges always