isual indicator (icon) placement in headers"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"row_details_accessible_affordance","decision":"Do not make the entire row the only interactive control. Add a dedicated "View details" link/button in the first cell (Date column) for each row; it is keyboard focusable and activates on Enter/Space. The accessible name is "View transaction details for {merchantName} on {date}". Row click may still activate details with pointer, but keyboard users use the dedicated control.","rationale":"A dedicated interactive element provides clear semantics, focusability, and a screen-reader label without turning <tr> into a custom control. Allowing pointer row-click preserves the brief behavior while ensuring full keyboard accessibility.","sourceGap":"Row click to open details lacks an accessible affordance (keyboard activation, focusability, and clear label for screen readers)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"table_loading_empty_error_states","decision":"Implement three explicit render states in the table body: (1) Loading: show 10 skeleton rows matching the current column layout and disable sorting/pagination controls; (2) Empty: show a single full-width row with message "No transactions to display"; (3) Error: show a single full-width row with message "Transactions failed to load" and a "Retry" button that re-triggers the last fetch with current sort/page/pageSize.","rationale":"These states cover the missing operational scenarios (fetching, no data, failure) with concrete UI outputs and control behavior, enabling deterministic tests and consistent UX across sort/paginate transitions.","sourceGap":"Loading state while fetching transactions (initial load and during sort/paginate)"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"pagination_model_and_disabled_boundaries","decision":"Pagination provides First, Previous, Next, Last buttons plus a page size selector (25/50/100). Display text: "Page X of Y" and "Z results". Changing page size resets to page 1. First/Previous are disabled on page 1; Next/Last are disabled on the final page. Disabled controls are not focusable.","rationale":"This fixes boundary behavior and defines a concrete pagination model and reset rule, keeping the control set minimal while supporting the required page sizes and clear user feedback.","sourceGap":"Specify pagination model: show total count, page count, and whether page size change resets to page 1; define available controls (first/prev/next/last, direct page input) and their labels"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"pagination_accessible_labels_and_live_updates","decision":"Add accessible labels: pagination nav has aria-label "Transaction pagination"; page size selector has label "Rows per page"; First/Prev/Next/Last buttons have aria-labels "First page", "Previous page", "Next page", "Last page". Add an aria-live="polite" status region within the table container that announces "Sorted by {column} {direction}" on sort and "Page {x} of {y}" on page changes.","rationale":"Explicit labeling and polite announcements address screen-reader discoverability and feedback for dynamic updates without overcomplicating the interaction model.","sourceGap":"Pagination controls lack labeling for screen readers (current page, total pages/results, page size selector label) and focus order expectations"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table","transaction_table_pagination"],"code":"focus_visible_requirements","decision":"Apply consistent :focus-visible styling to sortable header buttons, the "View details" control, and all pagination controls: 2px outline using the app focus color, 2px offset, and maintain at least 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors. Do not remove default outlines unless replaced by this rule.","rationale":"This creates a concrete, testable focus requirement for all interactive elements mentioned in the gaps and avoids relying on browser defaults that may be overridden by component styling.","sourceGap":"No focus-visible styling requirements specified for sortable headers, rows, and pagination controls"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table_status_badge"],"code":"status_badge_contrast_and_noncolor_redundancy","decision":"Badges always render the status text (Pending/Completed/Failed/Refunded) and must meet WCAG 2.1 AA contrast for text against badge background (>=4.5:1). If a chosen background cannot meet contrast with the intended text color, use a neutral background with a 2px left border in the status color and standard text color to preserve meaning without relying on low-contrast fills.","rationale":"Text provides non-color reinforcement, and the contrast rule plus fallback prevents inaccessible color pairings while preserving status differentiation in a conservative way.","sourceGap":"Status badges rely on color; no non-color reinforcement specified beyond text and no guidance for contrast-compliant badge/background pairings"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"cell_overflow_truncation_rules","decision":"Merchant Name and Payment Method cells are single-line with truncation (CSS ellipsis). On hover and keyboard focus (within cell), show a native tooltip via title attribute containing the full value. Row height remains fixed to a single line.","rationale":"This defines deterministic overflow handling on narrow widths without introducing complex custom tooltip components, and it remains accessible via focus-triggered title for keyboard users.","sourceGap":"Long-content overflow state for merchant name and payment method (truncate/wrap) and tooltip behavior if used"},{"affectedComponentCodes":["transaction_table"],"code":"responsive_table_horizontal_scroll_and_column_priority","decision":"On small screens, keep the table layout and enable horizontal scrolling within the table container (overflow-x: auto). Columns remain in the same order and are not hidden; minimum widths: Date 120px, Amount 120px, Status 120px, Merchant Name 200px, Payment Method 160px.","rationale":"Horizontal scroll is the least risky responsive strategy for a data table because it preserves all data and interactions without inventing a card layout or column hiding behavior not specified in the brief.","sourceGap":"No behavior defined for small screens: whether the table becomes horizontally scrollable, columns collapse, or transforms into a stacked/card layout"}]},"unitTests":{"components":[{"componentCode":"transaction_table_status_badge","componentName":"Transaction Status Badge","coveredBehaviors":["Renders the correct human-readable label for each supported status (pending/completed/failed/refunded)","Exposes status text in the accessible name (not color-only meaning)","Applies a status-specific styling hook (via class or data attribute) so status can be colored by CSS","Merges optional class_name with the component's base styling hook"],"coveredStates":["Pending","Completed","Failed","Refunded"],"files":[{"filename":"/app/generated/frontend/src/components/TransactionTableStatusBadge/TransactionTableStatusBadge.spec.tsx","content":"import React from 'react';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
